briefs.borrows:
Most-cited judges' fixes first, with the lenses that asked:
1. Plans needs a figure. Asked by feedback, soul, style, system and skeptic; usability and skeptic also asked for NOW on the Plans list. Soul's exact words were 'the lit NOW line crossing the month grid on today's row'; system asked for 'a week strip aligned to the calendar… with NOW and a lamp on each plan day'. Answered by the week rail and the Plans-list rail.
2. Kind words from 12px tracked caps to 13-14px sentence case: feedback, style, system, interaction, type and skeptic.
3. Home's Fig. 1:
- light and number the next stop (feedback);
- trim it to the rows (interaction);
- label each stop with its day (usability);
- plans only, aligned row by row with Coming up, no legend (skeptic);
- stops at the rows' pitch (style, on Live Figures);
- run NOW across Home's Coming up and To do (feedback, usability, interaction, skeptic).
4. Head links in bone with a 1px blueprint underline and arrow, blue kept for prose (feedback, style; system keeps blueprint links).
5. The dark bands under the Chat and Status heads and the empty Settings column (feedback, system, interaction, skeptic). The Settings column is filled with the needs-a-look link (interaction).
6. 'Here' as a 2px cap over a low tint instead of the steel slab, including 'Every kind' (feedback, style, skeptic). This borrows T1-32, the latched 'here' from track-refine.
7. Chat:
- the diagram as a gutter at the thread's pitch (system);
- light the arrow of the line pointed at (interaction);
- the diagram added nothing (usability), and now sits on its lines;
- her screen's bloom and the newest arrow's afterglow (skeptic).
8. Status's spend as a small lit tube (soul, feedback, skeptic), built as the original's own E15 character bar.
9. Pointing at a row lights its mark and fades over 1.2s (soul; system asked for it from figure-graft).
10. The kit's two-layer halo on the NOW line and every lit mark (soul, feedback).
11. Greeting:
- the tube moves right so the title is read first (interaction);
- the pool is squared and sized so there is no dead band (system);
- the scanlines are checked (soul).
12. Usability and type details:
- '#4' ids off the task titles (usability);
- a neutral tick with an amber edge bar (usability; borrows T1-16 from console-refine);
- READY as plain words (interaction);
- three 44px phone links instead of the summary disclosure (interaction);
- 'Show one kind' as the label, with keys on the phone (usability);
- drive time right-aligned and tabular, compass in its own column (type);
- eyebrows and column heads 13px semibold sentence case (type);
- curly apostrophes (type);
- an aligned '#n' column and the tagline hung on the grid (type);
- a 24px line (type, system);
- 'Edit' instead of 'Edit, complete or snooze' (tour lessons).
13. The tally's next-due drawn as a lit outline on its bar (system).
14. 'Coming up' counted after Next up (T1-42) and each count said once (tour lessons).

briefs.hypothesis:
Lit Manual's grammar (a plate, a figure from the page's own data, one lit mark) won heat b. Where it is still thin, it has nothing to draw:
- Plans has no figure;
- the month is an empty grid;
- Status's spend is a flat bar;
- the kinds are words in caps;
- 'in 4 days' is a bare phrase.

Four small devices from designs that finished low fill those places. Each speaks a manual's own grammar: an instrument's round gauge, a drawing's break line, a pencil-hatched legend and a draughtsman's dimension. Each gives its place a figure made from the page's own data and replaces what is there rather than sitting beside it, the pattern the tour's lessons say takes. They put the original's glass back on the two pages without a green screen, and put grounded, low-chroma colour into drawn things with a job.

Live Figures tried the round tube and failed with it. Here the tube goes only where it holds a number the page does not print, with words at a size that reads, and never in amber on To do. The lineage's main fixes are taken as the refinement takes them, so the two briefs differ in these devices, not in their care.
